35548	{"artifactId":"DEF-c66d49bb81925886","entry":{"id":"review-72e2978ce9cfc1205d6807b3cb78edf3","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:20:14.874Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"define","stage":"define","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"p01","ref":"4/c5","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"An approved common-artifact design supplies a reusable uniform artifact store and durable-history substrate.","evidence":"HLD.md:70 declares ArtifactStore, and S002/LLD.md:689 describes the shared envelope, decoder, store and History. plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:13 identifies S004/LLD.md and describes durable sidecars, a file journal and a per-repository store/service registry. These support the design's reusable store and durable-history scope, but the supplied evidence contains no approval record establishing that the design is approved.","action":"Verify the referenced design's approval status, or qualify the premise to describe the documented design without asserting approval.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The design scope is supported; its approval status is unverified. No concrete build-breaking contradiction is established.","options":["Supply an approval record for the referenced common-artifact design.","Reword the premise to say that the common-artifact design specifies a reusable uniform artifact store and durable-history substrate."]}},{"claimId":"p02","ref":"4/c6","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Artifact content hashing covers description, body and citations while allowing usage metadata to remain outside the hashed content boundary.","evidence":"The supplied read of plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review2-evidence.txt:1 includes the actual implementation at src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:103: contentHash hashes canonicalJson({ description, body: payload.body, citations: payload.citations }). Metadata, including meta.tokenUsage, is outside that explicit hashed object. This confirms the stated boundary; it does not establish metadata preservation by all writers.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p03","ref":"4/c7","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shared provider response permits usage to be absent.","evidence":"The supplied read of plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review2-evidence.txt:1 reproduces src/shared/types.ts:61–87: LLMResponse declares `usage?: { inputTokens: number; outputTokens: number; cacheReadTokens?: number | undefined; cacheCreationTokens?: number | undefined; } | undefined`. Both the optional property marker and explicit undefined permit usage to be absent.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p04","ref":"4/c7","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"When shared provider response usage exists, inputTokens and outputTokens are required and cache counters are optional.","evidence":"The supplied read of plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review2-evidence.txt:1 includes the actual LLMResponse declaration at src/shared/types.ts:61–87: usage is optional, but its object requires `inputTokens: number` and `outputTokens: number`; `cacheReadTokens?: number | undefined` and `cacheCreationTokens?: number | undefined` are optional. This confirms the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p05","ref":"1","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Provider response usage alone does not establish a durable artifact-level history across retries, interruption, corrections and rewrites.","evidence":"The supplied source excerpt at src/shared/types.ts:61–87 defines LLMResponse.usage as optional input/output/cache counters, without artifact ownership, attempt identity, persistence or correction history. plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review2-evidence.txt:1 explicitly distinguishes these counters from a durable per-call ledger and requires separate append/recovery, correction and rewrite-preservation contracts. The supplied lifecycle.ts:103 implementation hashes description, body and citations; it does not establish usage-history durability. These observations support the limited claim that provider response usage alone is insufficient.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p06","ref":"3","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"TU2 owns automatic workflow/provider capture and native Claude, Codex and Ollama usage normalization.","evidence":"plans/model-token-usage-implementation.md:31 assigns TU2 workflow capture context, provider normalization and dispatch/result instrumentation; :62 specifies automatic capture for daemon-dispatched model requests; :67 explicitly assigns normalization of supported Ollama, Claude CLI and Codex CLI usage; :74 assigns daemon instrumentation and provider-specific extraction to TU2. This confirms planned ownership, without asserting implementation already exists.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p07","ref":"3","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"TU3 owns controller-host capability negotiation, reporting and integrations.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review2-evidence.txt:1 includes the roadmap assigning TU3 'Reporting handshake, IPC/MCP ingestion, host integration and source coverage'; its contract-ownership table assigns 'Controller capability declarations and report ingestion' to TU3. The TU3 scope boundary explicitly owns external reporting and host integrations. These excerpts confirm the premise's planning ownership.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p08","ref":"3","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"TU4 owns task/story/epic hierarchy read models, including subtree usage totals and DeliverySnapshot integration.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review2-evidence.txt:1 explicitly assigns TU4 artifact/task/story/epic totals, canonical ownership aggregation, and extension of the delivery read contract with usage summaries and a usage watermark. It assigns ownership rollups and usage snapshots to TU4, while excluding work-item subtree totals from TU1. The same evidence identifies DeliverySnapshot as the existing daemon source of parent/child identities and artifact evidence. These excerpts confirm the proposed ownership boundary; TU4 remains proposed, not implemented.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p09","ref":"3","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"TU5 owns client presentation of usage, including board UI.","evidence":"plans/model-token-usage-implementation.md:34 assigns TU5 the Delivery board usage experience, including client contract consumption, summaries and Usage drill-downs. The supplied read of plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review2-evidence.txt:1 explicitly states: “TU5 owns presentation and client interaction” and assigns “Delivery board presentation and interaction” to TU5. This confirms the premise as planned ownership, not completed implementation.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p10","ref":"3","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The governing PRD scopes this work to token accounting and provenance rather than pricing, invoice reconciliation, budgets, inference interception, automatic model downgrades or raw prompt/response retention.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review2-evidence.txt:1 includes PRD §03, which excludes provider invoice reconciliation, dollar pricing, budgets, quota enforcement, automatic model downgrades, general machine traffic interception and storing prompts/completions. PRD §08 requires bounded normalized facts rather than raw prompt/response transcripts. The TU1 scope boundary assigns storage and accounting semantics to TU1 and excludes provider instrumentation, dispatch-site decisions, subtree totals and board UI. These excerpts support the stated accounting and provenance boundary.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p11","ref":"4/c2","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The PRD permits disclosed aggregate or unknown observation granularity without fabricating physical-call facts.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review2-evidence.txt:1 includes PRD §06: invocation-only per-model totals retain their granularity with physical call count unavailable; aggregate-only integration cannot claim complete per-call coverage. PRD §02 requires exposing actual granularity rather than relabeling invocation totals as model-call counts. §11 explicitly disclaims exact physical-call reconstruction when the source does not expose it, and TU11 requires unknown native model/call counts to remain unknown. These excerpts confirm the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p12","ref":"5/k1","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"Source c1 requires canonical append-only usage history in the owning artifact JSON at meta.tokenUsage, with pending storage serving only recovery.","evidence":"docs/model-token-usage-prd.html:562 explicitly places the canonical collection in artifact JSON and describes the pending outbox/journal as recovery, not an alternative final usage store. The supplied read of plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review2-evidence.txt:1 confirms the additive meta.tokenUsage.events collection and append-only contract. plans/model-token-usage-implementation.md:17 independently states the same placement and recovery boundary; DEF.md:72 records this as k1 citing c1.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p13","ref":"5/k2","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"Source c1 requires one stable identity and charged owner per actual model attempt, idempotent transport replay and distinct accounting for actual model retries.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review2-evidence.txt:1 explicitly states that a model attempt has exactly one callId, one charged artifact and one owning work item; multiple attempts of a logical request are distinct physical calls and count separately. Its durability requirements preserve stable event IDs across retries, acknowledge identical duplicates without another charge, and require retrying the append rather than the model call after recording failure. These source requirements confirm the premise; they do not assert existing implementation.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p14","ref":"5/k3","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"Source c3 requires preservation of original observations and visible conflicts for invalid references, conflicting identities, correction forks, cycles and unresolved reconciliation or attribution.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review2-evidence.txt:1 explicitly requires preserving original corrections; partial/conflict notices for cycles, forks, mismatched owners and nonexistent targets; visible conflicts for conflicting event IDs and concurrent branches; and preservation of both branches until reconciliation. Its ownership and token-semantics excerpts also require visible pending attribution, notices for ambiguous identities, retained reconciliation provenance, and disclosure of attribution mismatches. These requirements support the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p15","ref":"5/k4","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"Source c2 requires distinct measurement states, disjoint cache buckets, no duplicate reasoning counts, no summation of cumulative snapshots and no inferred observed physical-call count from aggregate evidence.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review2-evidence.