r schema rewrite, and transfers that do not duplicate charges.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-root-storage-decision.json:1 requires one data file per root artifact, appending root and child records, external usage storage, and daemon-owned DuckDB reporting. It does not establish the claimed evidence states, measurable limits, truncation/rotation/schema-rewrite prohibitions, or charge deduplication during transfers. Those requirements are unverifiable from the supplied evidence.","action":"Narrow the premise to the recorded decision or supply evidence explicitly establishing the additional requirements.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The cited decision supports the storage architecture but does not substantiate the additional constraints; their intended authority needs confirmation.","options":["Reword the premise to cover only the storage and reporting requirements explicitly recorded in the cited decision.","Retain the additional constraints and cite evidence that explicitly establishes them."]}},{"claimId":"p24","ref":"k10","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The roadmap permits TU1 completion on validated accounting services, producer contracts and preservation/recovery evidence independently of later capture, controller, hierarchy and board epics.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/roadmap.txt:1 explicitly states that an epic's completion must not depend on an unfinished successor. TU1 has no required predecessors and excludes provider instrumentation, subtree totals and board UI. Its exit criteria require durable accounting, preservation, recovery fixtures and accepted append/read contracts for TU2–TU4. The wave-1 gate requires accepted accounting/recovery/preservation contracts and settled provider/host feasibility boundaries; capture, controller reporting, hierarchy and board integration belong to TU2–TU5.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p25","ref":"s1/Extends","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The c11 grounding bundle contains relevant existing-code evidence supporting s1's immutable observation and reconciliation scope without claiming that the proposed accounting implementation already exists.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/grounding.json:1 identifies ArtifactStore (store.ts:102–417), decodeArtifactHead (decode.ts:81–133), createRepoLifecycle (repo-lifecycle.ts:27–35), and prepareArtifactWrite (storage.ts:254–310) as existing substrate. Its summary explicitly describes usage identity/schema, correction/reconciliation semantics, and append-only metadata preservation as new work. It also distinguishes optional LLMResponse from a persisted usage ledger and explicitly limits graph coverage and preservation claims. This supports the stated scope without claiming the accounting implementation exists.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p26","ref":"s2/Extends","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The c11 grounding bundle contains relevant existing-code evidence supporting s2's root ledger and identity reservation scope without claiming that the proposed accounting implementation already exists.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/grounding.json:1 identifies existing ArtifactStore, decodeArtifactHead, createRepoLifecycle and prepareArtifactWrite symbols, and filesystem profiles confirm store.ts and journal.ts exist. The bundle explicitly distinguishes the proposed usage identity/schema and accounting domain from existing lifecycle/history infrastructure, and states that LLMResponse is not evidence of a persisted usage ledger. It also acknowledges incomplete graph coverage and requires direct source reads during design. This confirms relevant substrate grounding without claiming the proposed accounting implementation exists.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p27","ref":"s3/Extends","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The c11 grounding bundle contains relevant existing-code evidence supporting s3's lifecycle preservation and ledger transfer scope without claiming that the proposed accounting implementation already exists.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/grounding.json:1 identifies ArtifactStore, decodeArtifactHead, createRepoLifecycle and prepareArtifactWrite as existing substrate. Its S002/S004 document excerpts describe uniform storage and durable lifecycle history. The bundle explicitly says TU1 should preserve generic lifecycle/history and proposes a separate usage-accounting domain; LLMResponse is expressly not evidence of a persisted ledger. These support the stated scope without claiming the proposed accounting exists. Graph coverage limitations and the need for direct source reads are explicitly retained.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p28","ref":"s4/Extends","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The c11 grounding bundle contains relevant existing-code evidence supporting s4's daemon accounting and operational qualification scope without claiming that the proposed accounting implementation already exists.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/grounding.json:1 supports reuse of ArtifactStore, its journal, decodeArtifactHead and prepareArtifactWrite, and explicitly describes usage accounting as a proposed separate domain. However, the bundle focuses on TU1 artifact storage and lifecycle foundations; it supplies no daemon accounting or operational qualification probes, and STORY-c66d49bb81925886-s4's scope was not provided. The claimed support for that specific scope is therefore unverifiable.","action":"Supply s4's scope and grounding probes covering its daemon accounting and operational qualification requirements, or narrow the premise to the artifact storage and lifecycle foundations actually evidenced.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence supports the substrate and proposed-versus-existing distinction, but cannot establish relevance to the unprovided s4 scope.","options":["Retain the premise after adding s4's scope and direct evidence for daemon accounting and operational qualification.","Narrow the premise to the bundle's verified artifact storage and lifecycle reuse foundations."]}},{"claimId":"p29","ref":"s2/Depends on","kind":"ordering","severity":"MED","premise":"The artifact declares s2 dependent on s1's usage identity and reconciliation semantics.","evidence":"No probes were run for this premise. No matches or read lines establish that s2 depends on s1's usage identity and reconciliation semantics; the premise is unverifiable.","action":"Gather the dependency declarations and relevant semantics from both story artifacts, then verify the stated ordering.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The supplied evidence supports neither confirming nor correcting the dependency.","options":["Probe both story artifacts to verify the dependency and its rationale.","Have the artifact author confirm or revise the dependency after reviewing both stories."]}},{"claimId":"p30","ref":"s3/Depends on","kind":"ordering","severity":"MED","premise":"The artifact declares s3 dependent on s2's durable root ledger and identity reservation foundation.","evidence":"No probes were run for this premise. No artifact reads or source evidence were supplied to verify that s3 depends on s2's durable root ledger and identity reservation foundation.","action":"Read the s2 and s3 artifacts and verify that s2 supplies the foundation required by s3 and that s3 declares this dependency.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The dependency is unverifiable from the supplied evidence; no evidence-derived text correction is safe.","options":["Gather s2 and s3 artifact evidence and retain the dependency if confirmed.","Revise the dependency after artifact evidence establishes the actual prerequisite."]}},{"claimId":"p31","ref":"s4/Depends on","kind":"ordering","severity":"MED","premise":"The artifact declares s4 dependent on both s2's ledger persistence and s3's lifecycle preservation and transfer behavior.","evidence":"No probes were run. No artifact reads or matches were supplied to verify s4's declared dependencies on s2 and s3.","action":"Read s4's Depends on declaration and the referenced s2 and s3 artifacts to verify the dependency ordering.","fixability":"manual","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The supplied evidence cannot establish the dependency declaration or support a safe text correction.","options":["Gather the dependency declaration and referenced story evidence, then reassess.","Revise the dependency ordering after reviewing s2, s3, and s4."]}},{"claimId":"p32","ref":"s4/ac6","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The existing daemon includes a DuckDB query layer that the proposed committed accounting snapshots are intended to serve.","evidence":"AGENTS.md:39 and CLAUDE.md:39 confirm an in-memory DuckDB query engine backing db_file_* tools. design/analyze-framework-data.md:498 describes file datasets queried through an in-process DuckDB pool. However, the supplied truncated matches do not establish any connection between that layer and the proposed committed accounting snapshots, or substantiate E20261026c66d49bb:S004:FR002. The full premise is therefore unverifiable.","action":"Supply evidence defining how committed accounting snapshots serve the DuckDB query layer, or narrow the premise to the evidenced existence of that layer.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The existing query layer is supported; its intended relationship to accounting snapshots needs additional grounding or an approved narrowing.","options":["Provide the referenced requirement and evidence specifying the snapshot-to-DuckDB integration.","Narrow the premise to: The existing daemon includes an in-memory DuckDB query layer backing the dat