26535	{"artifactId":"DEF-c66d49bb81925886","entry":{"id":"review-45ff9147a313502dc6f2d151d76bbd5d","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T06:30:01.345Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"define","stage":"define","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"p01","ref":"4/c16","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing ArtifactIds and decoded artifact envelopes provide canonical artifact identity and optional parent contracts.","evidence":"src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:48-93 defines ArtifactKey and per-kind identity shapes; :175-202 uses ArtifactIds.make and defines parentOf for TASK/TASKS/DIAG → STORY and STORY → EPIC. src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts:25-47 defines Artifact.id and optional parent: Reference. decode.ts:110-132 validates a supplied parent reference and preserves it in the decoded envelope. store.ts:392-407 validates parent artifact identity, requires derived-from, and enforces the canonical parent where parentOf supplies one. These reads confirm canonical identity and optional parent contracts.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p02","ref":"4/c16","kind":"closed-union","severity":"LOW","premise":"ArtifactIds.parentOf defines only TASK, TASKS and DIAG to STORY parent mappings and STORY to EPIC parent mappings.","evidence":"The read of plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/identity-parent.txt:1 includes src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:175-202: parentOf maps TASK, TASKS and DIAG to STORY, maps STORY to EPIC, and returns undefined in the default branch. Matches at src/workflow/__tests__/artifact-ids.test.ts:53-61 corroborate these mappings and undefined results for EPIC and LLD.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p03","ref":"4/c16","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon registry owns existing artifact lifecycle services.","evidence":"src/daemon/lifecycle-registry.ts:1-55 explicitly defines a per-repository lifecycle registry owning an ArtifactStore, LifecycleService, FeedbackService, and shared IdentityService. lifecycleFor resolves the repository path, returns a cached entry when present, otherwise calls createRepoLifecycle(repoPath), constructs the services, and caches the entry in ENTRIES. This confirms the daemon registry owns existing artifact lifecycle services.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p04","ref":"4/c16","kind":"closed-union","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing identity and parent contracts do not constitute a complete usage-root resolver covering document kinds, standalone work and reserved identities.","evidence":"src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:48-93 defines document kinds including DEF, HLD, SPEC, ISSUE, LLD and PLAN, while :175-202 implements parentOf only for TASK/TASKS/DIAG → STORY and STORY → EPIC; all other kinds return undefined. src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts:25-47 makes parent optional, and store.ts:392-407 validates a supplied parent without requiring one or resolving a usage root. These contracts therefore do not provide complete usage-root resolution across the stated cases. The truncated grep is not evidence of repository-wide absence.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p05","ref":"4/c6","kind":"inventory","severity":"LOW","premise":"Artifact content hashing covers description, body and citations.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c6.txt:1 shows contentHash in src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts hashing canonicalJson({ description, body: payload.body, citations: payload.citations }) with SHA-256, confirming all three fields are covered.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p06","ref":"4/c7","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shared provider response permits usage to be absent.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c7.txt:1 shows the shared LLMResponse interface declaring `usage?: { inputTokens: number; outputTokens: number; cacheReadTokens?: number | undefined; cacheCreationTokens?: number | undefined; } | undefined`, confirming usage may be absent.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p07","ref":"4/c7","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"When shared provider response usage exists, inputTokens and outputTokens are required and cache counters are optional.","evidence":"The read at plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c7.txt:1 shows LLMResponse declaring `usage?: { inputTokens: number; outputTokens: number; cacheReadTokens?: number | undefined; cacheCreationTokens?: number | undefined; } | undefined`. Thus, when usage exists, inputTokens and outputTokens are required and both cache counters are optional.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p08","ref":"4/c7","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A provider response usage object alone does not establish durable artifact-level accounting coverage.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c7.txt:1 reproduces LLMResponse from src/shared/types.ts: usage is optional and contains only inputTokens, outputTokens, cacheReadTokens and cacheCreationTokens. This response shape supplies neither artifact attribution nor a durability guarantee, confirming the narrow premise that usage alone does not establish durable artifact-level accounting coverage. The truncated grep provides no broader coverage guarantee.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p09","ref":"4/c2","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The cited PRD evidence permits disclosed aggregate or unknown measurement evidence without fabricated physical-call facts.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c2.txt:1 explicitly permits per-model invocation totals with “physical call count unavailable,” retains aggregates as fallback evidence, and requires reported, estimated, and unknown values to remain separate. It also prohibits backfilled guesses and states that aggregate-only integration does not satisfy complete per-call coverage. These provisions confirm the premise's allowance for disclosed aggregate or unknown evidence without fabricated physical-call facts.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p10","ref":"4/c17","kind":"ordering","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed s2 implementation depends on the identity and reconciliation rules established by s1.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/dependencies.json:1 explicitly lists s2.dependsOn as [\"s1\"]. Its s2 rationale states that durable submissions require s1 stable IDs, immutable event schema, and dedup/reconciliation semantics before persistence can validate a record. This confirms the proposed ordering without asserting implementation or approval.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p11","ref":"4/c17","kind":"ordering","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed s3 implementation depends on the acknowledged ledger and identity reservations established by s2.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/dependencies.json:1 explicitly lists s3.dependsOn as [\"s2\"]. Its s2 requirements include durable acknowledgment and canonical identities with root/child reservations; its s3 rationale states that lifecycle/import/transfer operates on s2 acknowledged root ledgers and stable reserved owners, so s2 must exist first. The file identifies these as proposed contract handoffs, consistent with the premise's proposed implementation ordering.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p12","ref":"4/c17","kind":"ordering","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed s4 implementation depends on s2 persistence and s3 lifecycle and transfer guarantees.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/dependencies.json:1 explicitly lists s4.dependsOn as [\"s2\",\"s3\"]. Its s4 rationale states that daemon submission/read and operational qualification expose the s2 storage contract and s3 independent lifecycle/transfer guarantees, confirming the proposed ordering.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p13","ref":"4/c17","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The dependency evidence records proposed build order and handoff rationale rather than asserting the existence of implemented story artifacts.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/dependencies.json:1 explicitly states \"proposed contract handoffs; no story implementation or approval asserted\". Its source names proposed story scope and ordered roadmap steps; s1–s4 define dependsOn relationships, and the rationale explains the s2, s3 and s4 handoffs. This confirms proposed build order without claiming implemented story artifacts.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p14","ref":"k1","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The cited stakeholder evidence requires one external root data file shared by descendants, which k1 proposes to implement as an Avro root ledger.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c1.txt:1 explicitly requires usage outside artifact documents, with “one append-only Avro object container file” at <project>/.insrc/usage/<root-artifact-id>/events.avro, and states: “All usage for the root and its descendants goes into this file.” This directly confirms the premise’s shared external root Avro ledger requirement.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p15","ref":"k2","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The c1 evidence supports distinguishing actual model attempts from transport replay, logical requests, native invocations, references and causal links for charging.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c1.txt:1 states that each model attempt has one callId and charge; a logical request may have multiple physical attempts, each counted. invocationId groups an invocation without a second charge, parentCallId is causal rather than additive, and references are not additional usage edges. It also explicitly excludes duplicate events and overlapping invocation/call observations from additional usage, supporting the transport-replay distinction.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p16","ref":"k3","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The c3 evidence supports preservation of original facts and explicit conflicts for invalid correction, reconciliation and attribution relationships.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 requires preserving original observations, with corrections and attribution transfers appending new facts. It explicitly requires partial/conflict notices for correction cycles, forks, mismatched owners and nonexistent targets; branch imports must validate root/owner/call identity and retain conflicting branches until reconciled. Cross-root transfers must reference the original event and be coordinated recoverably without a second charged call.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p17","ref":"k4","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The c2 evidence supports distinct measurement quality states, non-overlapping cache accounting, non-additive reasoning counters and non-additive cumulative snapshots.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c2.txt:1 explicitly separates reported, estimated and unknown usage, and distinguishes pending, unavailable, instrumented zero and legacy absence. It defines uncached input, cache reads and cache writes as separate buckets; reasoning as an informational subset of output that must never be added again; and session-cumulative counters as deltas against a durable baseline, stating “Never sum successive cumulative snapshots.” This confirms all four claims.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p18","ref":"k5","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The c3 evidence supports independent content and usage persistence with acknowledged history preserved through lifecycle and transfer operations.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 explicitly states that artifact writers and codecs do not own usage bytes, usage-only appends preserve content hashes and revision, and regeneration and approval leave ledger bytes intact. It requires durable acknowledgment, preservation of original observations, explicit retention/tombstone handling, paired import/export behavior, branch-history union by stable ID, and recoverably coordinated cross-root transfers without a second charged call. These requirements support the premise's independent persistence and history preservation through lifecycle and transfer operations.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p19","ref":"k6","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The c3 evidence supports durable acknowledgment, concurrent submission recovery and pre-content root and child identity reservations.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 explicitly requires acknowledgment only after the Avro block and required filesystem metadata are durable; serialization by repository and root ID; restart recovery of staged events using stable IDs; and idempotent duplicate acknowledgment with conflicting payload rejection. It also permits a root to reserve its stable ID and create its ledger before a valid artifact body exists, permits child events against reserved stable child IDs, and requires reconciliation of pending identities when documents are created. These requirements support the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p20","ref":"k7","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The c1 stakeholder evidence assigns review usage to the reviewed LLD, task usage to TASK and shared story validation and code-review usage to BUILD.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c1.txt:1 assigns LLD authoring, correction and design reviews to “the reviewed LLD as charged artifact”; task implementation, probes, repair and task validation are “charged to TASK”; story-wide validation and post-build code review are “charged to story BUILD”. These directly confirm the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p21","ref":"k8","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The cited conventions require daemon-owned persistence, sequential provider awaits, CLI-only cloud inference and critical-role model floors while documenting summary/index overlap.","evidence":"The read at plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/conventions.txt:1 reproduces AGENTS.md:1–150 and confirms all five claims: daemon ownership of DB access, serial for...of provider awaits, cloud inference through CLI subprocesses only, coreFloor protection for critical roles, and summary/index overlap limited to an already-running summary when code work arrives. AGENTS.md:12, :123 and :137 also directly corroborate the CLI and lane conventions.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p22","ref":"k9","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The c3 evidence supports explicit missing, legacy, unsupported and malformed accounting states and forbids silent history loss or duplicated transfer charges.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 explicitly requires import/export to disclose missing root-ledger data, forbids silent historical loss, and says cross-root transfers must not copy a second charged call. It also requires visible reporting outcomes for unavailable extensions and explicit failures for committed-history corruption. However, the supplied read does not establish explicit legacy, unsupported, and malformed accounting states as claimed.","action":"Narrow the premise to the accounting conditions explicitly supported by c3, or supply evidence defining the claimed legacy, unsupported, and malformed states.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The history-preservation and transfer-deduplication requirements are supported, but the full claimed state inventory is not verifiable from this evidence.","options":["Reword the premise around explicit missing-data disclosure, visible reporting failures, history preservation, and transfer deduplication.","Supply additional evidence defining explicit legacy, unsupported, and malformed accounting states."]}},{"claimId":"p23","ref":"k10","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The cited roadmap allows TU1 completion independently of later capture, controller, hierarchy and board epics.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/roadmap.txt:1 explicitly states that an epic's completion must not depend on an unfinished successor. The dependency table gives TU1 no required predecessors. TU1's scope excludes provider instrumentation, subtree totals and board UI, and its exit criteria require accepted contracts and deterministic fixtures for TU2–TU4. The build sequence places TU1 in wave 1 with its own acceptance gate, before capture, controller reporting, hierarchical queries and board integration.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p24","ref":"3","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The roadmap assigns automatic capture and provider normalization to TU2, controller integration to TU3, hierarchy read models to TU4 and client presentation to TU5.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/roadmap.txt:1 explicitly assigns workflow capture context, provider normalization and dispatch/result instrumentation to TU2; reporting handshake, IPC/MCP ingestion and host integration to TU3; ownership aggregation and usage query contracts to TU4; and client presentation and interaction to TU5. Its scope boundaries and contract ownership table confirm this division. plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/scope.txt:1 also confirms cooperating controllers report through the common capture contract where telemetry is available.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p25","ref":"3","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The PRD excludes monetary pricing, invoice reconciliation, budgets, inference interception, automatic model downgrades and raw prompt or completion retention.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/scope.txt:1 explicitly places provider invoice reconciliation, dollar pricing, budgets and automatic model downgrades outside the first release, along with intercepting general machine traffic and storing prompts/completions. These exclusions support the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p26","ref":"6.1/Extends","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The grounding bundle cited as c11 supports s1's extension of existing artifact infrastructure with immutable usage observation semantics.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/grounding.json:1 identifies ArtifactStore and its journal as reuse foundations and explicitly scopes new usage identity/schema, correction/reconciliation semantics, and append-only metadata preservation across store/decoder/lifecycle/storage boundaries. This supports extending existing infrastructure with the proposed immutable usage observations; it does not claim those semantics already exist. The bundle also explicitly limits graph coverage and requires direct source reads during design.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p27","ref":"6.2/Extends","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The grounding bundle cited as c11 supports s2's extension of existing artifact infrastructure with root-ledger persistence.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/grounding.json:1 explicitly identifies ArtifactStore and its journal as reuse foundations for TU1's separate usage-accounting domain. Its S002/LLD.md excerpts describe uniform artifact storage and a required WriteJournal; S004/LLD.md excerpts describe durable history and recovery of interrupted writes. This supports extending existing infrastructure with root-ledger persistence, without establishing exhaustive caller coverage or detailed preservation guarantees.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p28","ref":"6.3/Extends","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The grounding bundle cited as c11 supports s3's extension of existing lifecycle infrastructure with independent usage preservation and transfer.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/grounding.json:1 supports reuse of ArtifactStore, its journal and durable lifecycle history, and identifies usage accounting as a separate new domain. However, its limitations explicitly state that direct source reads are required and that it makes 'no exhaustive absence or preservation claim.' Neither s3's contents nor evidence establishing independent usage preservation and transfer was supplied. The full premise is therefore unverifiable; no concrete build-breaking contradiction is established.","action":"Narrow the claim to reuse of existing lifecycle infrastructure, or supply direct evidence and s3 details establishing independent usage preservation and transfer.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The bundle supports substrate reuse but does not establish the stronger preservation and transfer claim.","options":["Reword the premise to claim only that c11 supports reuse of ArtifactStore, its journal and durable lifecycle history for a separate usage-accounting domain.","Retain the premise after adding direct source evidence and the relevant s3 requirements demonstrating independent usage preservation and transfer."]}},{"claimId":"p29","ref":"6.4/Extends","kind":"cross-a