41747	{"artifactId":"DEF-c66d49bb81925886","entry":{"id":"review-f698772be4a4fba8d9464e8f7528868a","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T06:41:42.579Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"define","stage":"define","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"p01","ref":"4/c16","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing ArtifactIds and decoded artifact envelopes provide canonical identity and optional parent information.","evidence":"The supplied identity-parent.txt:1 read confirms ArtifactKey's identity components and per-kind shapes in src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:48-93, and parentOf's optional parent derivation at :175-202. Artifact<P> declares id and optional parent: Reference in src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts:25-47. decode.ts:110-132 validates and preserves the optional envelope parent alongside id. store.ts:392-407 validates parent artifact identity, derived-from relation, and the expected parent where defined. These support the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p02","ref":"4/c16","kind":"closed-union","severity":"LOW","premise":"ArtifactIds.parentOf defines parent relationships only from TASK, TASKS and DIAG to STORY and from STORY to EPIC.","evidence":"The supplied read of src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:175-202 shows parentOf returning STORY for TASK, TASKS and DIAG, EPIC for STORY, and undefined for every other kind. Matches at src/workflow/__tests__/artifact-ids.test.ts:57-61 corroborate these mappings and undefined results for EPIC and LLD.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p03","ref":"4/c16","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon registry owns artifact lifecycle services.","evidence":"The supplied read includes src/daemon/lifecycle-registry.ts:1-55: RepoLifecycle holds an ArtifactStore, LifecycleService, FeedbackService and IdentityService. lifecycleFor canonicalizes the repository path, reuses its cached ENTRIES entry, or creates the store and service with createRepoLifecycle and caches them. This confirms the daemon registry owns per-repository artifact lifecycle services.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p04","ref":"4/c16","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Existing identity and parent contracts do not provide complete usage-root resolution for document kinds, standalone work and reserved identities.","evidence":"src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:175-202 defines parentOf only for TASK, TASKS, DIAG and STORY; all other kinds return undefined. src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts:25-47 makes parent optional, and store.ts:392-407 checks the expected parent only when both a parent and a parentOf result exist. These support incomplete document-kind parent resolution. However, the supplied evidence does not establish standalone-work or reserved-identity resolution behavior; the truncated grep cannot establish absence of another resolver.","action":"Narrow the premise to the demonstrated parent-contract limitation, or supply targeted evidence for standalone work and reserved identities before retaining the full claim.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The document-kind limitation is grounded, but the full semantic claim exceeds the supplied evidence.","options":["Narrow the premise to parentOf's limited kind coverage and the optional parent contract.","Retain the full premise after supplying targeted reads covering standalone-work and reserved-identity usage-root resolution."]}},{"claimId":"p05","ref":"4/c6","kind":"inventory","severity":"LOW","premise":"Artifact content hashing covers description, body and citations.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c6.txt:1 shows contentHash in src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts hashing canonicalJson({ description, body: payload.body, citations: payload.citations }) with SHA-256, confirming all three fields are covered.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p06","ref":"4/c7","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shared provider response permits usage to be absent.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c7.txt:1 shows the shared LLMResponse declaring `usage?: { inputTokens: number; outputTokens: number; cacheReadTokens?: number | undefined; cacheCreationTokens?: number | undefined; } | undefined`. Both the optional property marker and explicit undefined permit usage to be absent.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p07","ref":"4/c7","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"When shared provider response usage exists, inputTokens and outputTokens are required and cache counters are optional.","evidence":"The read at plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c7.txt:1 shows LLMResponse declaring `usage?: { inputTokens: number; outputTokens: number; cacheReadTokens?: number | undefined; cacheCreationTokens?: number | undefined; } | undefined`. Thus usage is optional; when present, inputTokens and outputTokens are required, and both cache counters are optional.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p08","ref":"4/c7","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Provider response usage by itself does not establish durable artifact-level accounting coverage.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c7.txt:1 reproduces src/shared/types.ts's LLMResponse: optional usage contains inputTokens, outputTokens and optional cache token counts, with no artifact identity or persistence contract. This supports the narrow premise that provider response usage alone does not establish durable artifact-level accounting coverage; it does not establish whether such coverage exists elsewhere.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p09","ref":"4/c2","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The cited PRD permits disclosed aggregate or unknown usage evidence without inventing per-call observations.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c2.txt:1 explicitly permits retaining per-model invocation totals with physical call count unavailable, treats aggregates as fallback evidence, and requires reported, estimated, and unknown usage to remain separate. It also says missing baselines yield unknown deltas and prohibits backfilling guesses. This confirms the premise; aggregate-only integration separately does not satisfy complete per-call coverage.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p10","ref":"4/c17","kind":"ordering","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed s2 implementation depends on the identity and reconciliation rules defined by s1.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/dependencies.json:1 explicitly lists s2.dependsOn as [\"s1\"]. Its s2 rationale states that durable submissions need s1 stable IDs, immutable event schema, and dedup/reconciliation semantics before persistence can validate a record. The file identifies these as proposed contract handoffs, matching the premise's proposed implementation scope.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p11","ref":"4/c17","kind":"ordering","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed s3 implementation depends on s2 providing acknowledged ledger persistence and identity reservations.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/dependencies.json:1 explicitly lists s3.dependsOn as [\"s2\"]. Its s2 requirements include durable acknowledgment and standalone/pre-content root/child reservations; its s3 rationale states that lifecycle/import/transfer behavior operates on s2 acknowledged root ledgers and stable reserved owners, so s2 must exist first. This confirms the proposed dependency without asserting implementation or approval.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p12","ref":"4/c17","kind":"ordering","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed s4 implementation depends on s2 persistence and s3 lifecycle and transfer guarantees.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/dependencies.json:1 explicitly lists s4.dependsOn as [\"s2\",\"s3\"]. Its s4 rationale states that daemon submission/read and operational qualification expose the s2 storage contract and s3 independent lifecycle/transfer guarantees. The file identifies these as proposed contract handoffs, matching the premise's proposed implementation scope.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p13","ref":"4/c17","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The dependency evidence describes proposed build order rather than already implemented story artifacts.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/dependencies.json:1 explicitly states \"proposed contract handoffs; no story implementation or approval asserted\" and identifies its source as \"Current DEF proposed story scope and implementation roadmap TU1 ordered steps\". The dependsOn entries and rationale describe the proposed ordering of s1–s4.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p14","ref":"3/TU2","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The roadmap assigns automatic capture, inference-dispatch instrumentation and native provider usage normalization to TU2 rather than TU1.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/roadmap.txt:1 explicitly assigns TU2 automatic daemon capture, “Normalize native provider usage,” and “Connect dispatch and completion to durable capture.” Its TU1 scope boundary states that TU1 does not instrument model providers or decide workflow dispatch sites, and that provider adapters belong to TU2. plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/scope.txt:1 describes release-wide capture coverage without contradicting that epic allocation.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p15","ref":"3/TU3","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The roadmap assigns controller capability negotiation, reporting and host integrations to TU3 rather than TU1.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/roadmap.txt:1 assigns TU3 the reporting handshake, IPC/MCP ingestion, host integration and source coverage. TU3 step 1 defines host capability declarations and the reporting handshake; the contract ownership table assigns controller capability declarations and report ingestion to TU3. TU1 owns storage and accounting semantics, including shared coverage semantics and measurement-boundary qualification. plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/scope.txt:1 confirms cooperating controllers submit usage through the shared capture contract and missing host counters remain unavailable.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p16","ref":"3/TU4-TU5","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The roadmap assigns hierarchical work read models to TU4 and client presentation to TU5, excluding subtree totals, DeliverySnapshot integration and board UI from TU1.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/roadmap.txt:1 assigns TU4 ownership aggregation, usage queries and snapshot consistency, including extending the delivery read contract with usage summaries and a watermark. It assigns TU5 client contract consumption, summaries and Usage drill-downs. TU1's scope boundary explicitly excludes work-item subtree totals and board UI. Together these boundaries support reserving delivery snapshot usage integration for TU4 and client presentation for TU5.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p17","ref":"3/common-artifact-store","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"TU1 is intended to reuse the common artifact identity, ownership, lifecycle, journal and content-storage contracts rather than replace them.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/integration-map.txt:1 explicitly defines reuse boundaries: existing canonical identities scope accounting owners, and existing content services continue owning artifact files while TU1 adds independent ledger behavior. Its source excerpts show ArtifactKey and parent rules (src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:48–93,175–202), the common artifact envelope and lifecycle (artifact-core/types.ts:25–47), parent validation (artifact-core/store.ts:392–407), and the shared per-repository store, history and lifecycle services (src/daemon/lifecycle-registry.ts:1–55). These support the stated intent to reuse existing contracts rather than replace them.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p18","ref":"3/PRD-exclusions","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The PRD excludes pricing, invoice reconciliation, budgets, automatic model downgrades, general inference interception and raw prompt or completion retention.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/scope.txt:1 explicitly places provider invoice reconciliation, dollar pricing, budgets, automatic model downgrades, intercepting general machine traffic, and storing prompts/completions outside the first release. plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/roadmap.txt:1 reinforces these boundaries: token accounting excludes pricing, billing, budgets and automatic model selection, and usage collection must not store prompts or completions.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p19","ref":"k1","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The cited stakeholder requirement calls for one external root data file shared by the root artifact and its descendants.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c1.txt:1 explicitly requires: “Store one append-only Avro object container file at <project>/.insrc/usage/<root-artifact-id>/events.avro” and “All usage for the root and its descendants goes into this file.” It also states “Keep usage outside artifact documents” and “One live file per root is the initial contract.” These confirm the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p20","ref":"k1","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed authoritative usage store is append-only events.avro under <project>/.insrc/usage/<root-artifact-id>/, while journals and Parquet caches are recovery or derived data.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c1.txt:1 explicitly specifies one append-only Avro object container at <project>/.insrc/usage/<root-artifact-id>/events.avro. It states that journals/checkpoints may support recovery but cannot become a second final ledger, and that DuckDB tables, indexes and Parquet caches are rebuildable while Avro remains authoritative. This confirms the proposed storage contract.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p21","ref":"k1","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every proposed usage event carries both rootArtifactId and the charged artifactId.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c1.txt:1 explicitly states: “Every record carries rootArtifactId, charged artifactId” and that outcomes and corrections retain the same root/charged identity. Its decoded example includes both fields on request.started and request.finished events. This confirms the premise about proposed events.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p22","ref":"k2","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed accounting identity assigns one stable call identity and one charged owner to each actual model attempt, preserving distinct retries while deduplicating transport replay.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c1.txt:1 explicitly assigns each model attempt exactly one callId, charged artifact and owning work item; distinguishes multiple attempts of a logical request as separate physical calls that count; and requires recovery using stable IDs. It also states that duplicate events and overlapping invocation/call observations are not additional usage, and that references do not duplicate charges. These provisions support distinct retry accounting and transport replay deduplication in the proposed contract.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p23","ref":"k2","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Logical requests, native invocations, reference records and causal links must not independently create additional consumption charges.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c1.txt:1 explicitly states that each physical model attempt counts, while invocationId groups an invocation and “is not a second charge”; parentCallId is causal, “not an ownership or summation edge”; review records reference call IDs without copying charges; and references are not additional usage edges. This confirms that logical grouping, invocations, reference records and causal links do not independently add charges.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p24","ref":"k3","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed effective-observation model retains original facts and treats invalid references, conflicting identities, forks and cycles as visible conflicts rather than silently replacing or adding contributions.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 explicitly requires preserving original observations, appending corrections and attribution transfers as new facts, and treating corrections as complete replacements rather than additive charges. It specifies partial/conflict notices for cycles, forks, mismatched owners and nonexistent targets; conflicting event-ID payloads are conflicts rather than last-writer-wins, and forked branch corrections remain visible until reconciled.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p25","ref":"k4","kind":"closed-union","severity":"LOW","premise":"The accounting contract distinguishes reported, estimated, pending, unavailable and historical not-recorded measurement states.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c2.txt:1 separates reported and estimated values, defines pending as a durable start without a terminal observation, defines unavailable as an attempt without usable counters, and labels legacy absence “Not recorded”. These confirm the stated distinctions; the same passage also discusses unknown usage.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p26","ref":"k4","kind":"external-contract","severity":"LOW","premise":"A source's cache, reasoning, cumulative and aggregate counters require qualified semantics before they can support non-overlapping totals or a physical-call count.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c2.txt:1 explicitly separates cache buckets, treats reasoning as a subset of inclusive output, requires cumulative counters to be differenced against a durable same-session/model baseline, and prohibits summing overlapping leaf and aggregate observations. It also states that invocation-level per-model totals leave physical call count unavailable. These requirements confirm that qualified source semantics are necessary before deriving non-overlapping totals or physical-call counts.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p27","ref":"k5","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed usage append operation changes ledger freshness without changing artifact JSON bytes, content hash, revision, status, approval or signoffs.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 explicitly specifies that usage appends advance a separate usage sequence/watermark, leave artifact files intact, do not invalidate approval or reset content revision, and remain independent of artifact regeneration and approval. This supports preserving artifact JSON, status and signoffs. plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c6.txt:1 shows contentHash hashes only canonical description, body and citations, which the proposed append leaves unchanged.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p28","ref":"k5","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Ordinary artifact regeneration, serialization and lifecycle writes must preserve external ledger bytes, while paired transfer and retention operations preserve acknowledged usage history.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 explicitly requires artifact writers/codecs to leave usage bytes intact, regeneration and approval to preserve the ledger, paired import/export to retain or disclose missing history, and retention to preserve an accounting owner. It also requires recoverable cross-root transfers without duplicate charging. plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/integration-map.txt:1 confirms these as proposed s3 requirements and acceptance checks ac2, ac3, ac5 and ac6, explicitly distinguishing them from existing capabilities.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p29","ref":"k6","kind":"ordering","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed daemon writer acknowledges acceptance only after complete Avro blocks and required directory metadata are durable.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 explicitly states: “Serialize by repository and root ID, append complete Avro blocks, and acknowledge only after the block and required filesystem metadata are durable.” This confirms the proposed writer's acceptance ordering; it does not establish an existing implementation.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p30","ref":"k6","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed writer serializes concurrent submissions per repository/root and recovers interrupted tails without losing acknowledged events.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 explicitly requires: “Serialize by repository and root ID,” append complete Avro blocks, and acknowledge only after the block and required filesystem metadata are durable. Its restart contract requires validating the completed prefix, detecting and isolating incomplete tails, and recovering staged events using stable IDs; corruption inside committed history is an explicit failure. These provisions confirm the proposed serialization and acknowledged-event preservation contract, though they do not demonstrate an implemented writer.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p31","ref":"k6","kind":"ordering","severity":"LOW","premise":"Stable root and child artifact identities must be reservable before content creation without fabricated artifact bodies or approvals, duplicate final ledgers or repeated inference.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 explicitly requires reserving a stable root ID and creating its ledger before a valid artifact body exists, targeting reserved child IDs, and reconciling identities without fabricated design content or rerunning inference. It also prohibits a recovery journal from becoming a second final ledger and states that regeneration and approval do not rewrite the ledger. identity-parent.txt:1 shows content-independent ArtifactKey fields (src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:48–93) and limited parentOf coverage (:175–202), consistent with requiring explicit reservation and ownership handling rather than assuming parentOf resolves every root.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p32","ref":"k7","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The stakeholder attribution rule charges design reviews to the reviewed LLD, task execution to TASK, and shared story validation and code review to BUILD.","evidence":"Not judged: the reviewing model call failed 3 times. Last error: codex stalled: no model output in 90 s (session 01a17719-1ac6-7e13-bac7-e86fb16096be); the run was killed","action":"Re-run the review, or judge this premise by hand.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p33","ref":"k7","kind":"ordering","severity":"MED","premise":"Dispatch-time ownership remains the attribution basis unless an explicit provenance-preserving transfer changes the effective owner.","evidence":"Not judged: the reviewing model call failed 3 times. Last error: codex stalled: no model output in 90 s (session 01a1771a-7da7-7f22-9ff5-5ced09e9d538); the run was killed","action":"Re-run the review, or judge this premise by hand.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p34","ref":"k8","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"AGENTS.md requires persistence access through daemon-owned interfaces.","evidence":"AGENTS.md:132 requires CLI, MCP, and workbench to access LMDB and LanceDB through daemon IPC. AGENTS.md:136 explicitly states that the daemon owns all DB access. The supplied read of plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/conventions.txt:1 reproduces both rules, confirming the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p35","ref":"k8","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"AGENTS.md requires sequential awaits for all provider operations and documents the permitted in-progress summary/index overlap.","evidence":"AGENTS.md:122 explicitly prohibits Promise.all for anything reaching an LLM provider and requires serial for...of with sequential awaits. AGENTS.md:123 documents that summaries start only while the index lane is idle, permitting overlap only when code work arrives during an already-running summary. plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/conventions.txt:1 reproduces both statements.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p36","ref":"k8","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"Project conventions require cloud inference through local Claude or Codex CLI subprocesses and enforce the critical-role model floor.","evidence":"AGENTS.md:12 and :137 require cloud access through local claude/codex CLI subprocesses via CliProvider and prohibit direct cloud REST. plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/conventions.txt:1 reproduces the critical-role coreFloor convention. docs/daemon.md:486–487 and :496–497 describe the minimum tier for critical roles and upward clamping to the effective coreFloor. These confirm the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p37","ref":"k9","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Absent, legacy, malformed and unsupported ledger evidence must produce explicit accounting quality states rather than a complete measured zero.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 explicitly defines legacy/not-recorded, missing, unsupported and malformed states, and states: “Each retains readable artifact content and produces an accounting notice rather than complete zero.” This directly confirms the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p38","ref":"k9","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The proposed single live root file has measured growth, read and recovery limits and cannot silently truncate, rotate or rewrite its schema.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 requires: “Set measurable size/read-recovery limits in TU1”; it supplies no measured limits or results. It does prohibit silent rotation, truncation and compaction, fixes the writer schema in the file header, and requires an explicit recoverable plan for incompatible writer-schema migration. The premise overstates established measurements, but the prescribed safeguards remain supported.","action":"Describe measurable limits as a TU1 requirement awaiting validation, rather than an already measured property.","fixability":"auto","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence directly supports a requirement, not completed measurement.","artifactEdits":[{"find":"The proposed single live root file has measured growth, read and recovery limits and cannot silently truncate, rotate or rewrite its schema.","replace":"The proposed single live root file requires measurable size/read-recovery limits to be set and validated in TU1; silent rotation, truncation and compaction are prohibited, and incompatible writer-schema migration requires an explicit recoverable plan before acceptance."}]}},{"claimId":"p39","ref":"k10","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"TU1 completion depends on validated accounting, preservation, recovery and producer contracts independently of later capture, controller, hierarchy and board implementations.","evidence":"Not judged: the reviewing model call failed 3 times. Last error: codex stalled: no model output in 90 s (session 01a1771b-e092-76d0-b82e-06580a1c0d69); the run was killed","action":"Re-run the review, or judge this premise by hand.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p40","ref":"s1/Extends","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The c11 grounding bundle supports s1's immutable observation identity and reconciliation scope.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/grounding.json:1 supports ArtifactStore/journal reuse and identifies new usage identity/schema and correction/reconciliation semantics as TU1 work. It does not specify immutable observation identity or s1's reconciliation boundaries. STORY-c66d49bb81925886-s1 was not supplied, so compatibility with that story cannot be verified. The bundle also explicitly requires direct source reads during design and disclaims exhaustive preservation claims.","action":"Supply s1's identity and reconciliation requirements with direct evidence supporting those requirements, or narrow the premise to the bundle's demonstrated substrate and broad TU1 scope.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence supports broad scope and substrate reuse, but does not establish the specific identity and reconciliation contract attributed to s1.","options":["Provide s1's relevant requirements and direct grounding for immutable identity and reconciliation boundaries.","Narrow the premise to ArtifactStore/journal reuse and the need to design new usage identity and reconciliation semantics."]}},{"claimId":"p41","ref":"s2/Extends","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The c11 grounding bundle supports s2's root-ledger persistence and identity reservation scope.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/grounding.json:1 identifies ArtifactStore and its journal as reuse foundations and describes a new usage-accounting identity/schema domain. It does not establish root-ledger persistence or identity reservation semantics, and no contents of STORY-c66d49bb81925886-s2 were supplied for comparison. The bundle explicitly says direct source reads are required during design and disclaims exhaustive coverage. The claimed cross-artifact support is therefore unverifiable.","action":"Supply s2's persistence and identity reservation requirements and direct source evidence supporting those requirements, or narrow the premise to the bundle's demonstrated substrate reuse.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence supports general substrate reuse, but cannot establish the specific s2 scope.","options":["Retain the premise after supplying s2 and direct evidence for root-ledger persistence and identity reservation.","Narrow the premise to ArtifactStore and journal reuse foundations, leaving s2's specific semantics to separate grounding."]}},{"claimId":"p42","ref":"s3/Extends","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The c20 integration map supports s3's artifact lifecycle, serialization and ledger-transfer integration scope.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/integration-map.txt:1 explicitly maps s3 to lifecycle preservation, kind-specific serialization and round-trip import/export (ac2), supersession (ac3), binary-safe reconciliation (ac4), and recoverable ownership transfer (ac6). It distinguishes these proposed additions from existing capabilities. Its source excerpts ground the reuse boundary: src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts:392-407 validates artifact links, and src/daemon/lifecycle-registry.ts:1-55 supplies repository-owned artifact and lifecycle services. Thus c20 supports the stated integration scope without claiming ledger preservation or transfer already exists.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p43","ref":"s4/Extends","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The c20 integration map supports s4's daemon accounting access and operational integration scope.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/integration-map.txt:1 explicitly maps c20 to s4's proposed scoped accounting append/read, watermarks, bounded access and compatibility tests, while stating these APIs and snapshot compatibility do not already exist. Its source excerpts support the reuse boundaries: src/daemon/lifecycle-registry.ts:1-55 provides canonical per-repository services; src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:48-93 defines artifact identities; src/daemon/db/drivers/duckdb-file.ts:85-145 routes Avro through conversion to Parquet; and src/daemon/db/drivers/converters/avro.ts:1-75 supplies the Avro converter foundation. The map retains compatibility qualification as implementation acceptance and excludes full reporting aggregation from TU1.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p44","ref":"s2/ac4","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A durably recorded attempt start without a usable final observation must recover as pending or interrupted with unavailable usage.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c2.txt:1 defines pending as a durable start without a terminal observation and unavailable as a terminal/interrupted attempt without usable counters; neither is measured zero. Its crash-recovery requirement, repeated in c3.txt:1, requires a durable start before dispatch and an interrupted/unknown attempt after a crash without usable counters. These directly support the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p45","ref":"s2/ac5","kind":"ordering","severity":"MED","premise":"Accounting persistence failure must be repairable by replaying recording without rerunning model inference.","evidence":"Not judged: the reviewing model call failed 3 times. Last error: codex stalled: no model output in 90 s (session 01a1771d-42db-7c70-a127-bb46dab943ae); the run was killed","action":"Re-run the review, or judge this premise by hand.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p46","ref":"s3/ac4","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Branch reconciliation must import binary ledger histories through the daemon, retaining distinct events once and surfacing conflicting IDs without text merges or timestamp-based winners.","evidence":"Not judged: the reviewing model call failed 3 times. Last error: codex stalled: no model output in 90 s (session 01a1771e-a6a2-7110-9c10-ab88e089a731); the run was killed","action":"Re-run the review, or judge this premise by hand.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p47","ref":"s3/ac6","kind":"ordering","severity":"LOW","premise":"Cross-root ownership transfers must recover interrupted durable steps so that transfer references reconcile once and unresolved gaps or duplicate charges cannot appear complete.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 explicitly requires cross-root transfers to reference the original event, be coordinated recoverably, and avoid copying a second charged call into the destination ledger. The same read requires stable-ID recovery of staged events, identical-duplicate acknowledgment without another charge, and missing or conflicting accounting data to produce notices rather than appear complete. These requirements support the premise's recovery, reconciliation, and completeness constraints.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p48","ref":"s4/ac2","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Accounting access must validate repository scope, artifact identity and ownership instead of allowing arbitrary file targets or invented attribution.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/integration-map.txt:1 explicitly defines proposed s4/ac2 to reject or hold unresolved invalid identity, wrong scope, unresolved ownership and arbitrary file targeting. Its source excerpts show canonical ID shapes in src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:48-93, parent-link validation in src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts:392-407 and canonical repository paths in src/daemon/lifecycle-registry.ts:1-55. plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 requires directory creation and root IDs to be validated against the registered repository, prohibits client-supplied arbitrary filesystem paths and forbids guessing roots from missing ownership links. The integration map explicitly identifies scoped accounting access as proposed work, not existing functionality.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p49","ref":"s4/ac3","kind":"ordering","severity":"LOW","premise":"Bounded ledger reads must traverse acknowledged history consistently at a recorded root watermark without silently omitting records.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 explicitly requires reading to an acknowledged root watermark while appends continue, using a bounded committed-prefix snapshot or coordinated reader lease and recording a watermark per root. It also states that corruption inside committed history must be an explicit failure, never silently skipped. These requirements support consistent bounded traversal without silent omissions; the truncated grep adds no implementation verification.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p50","ref":"s4/ac6","kind":"external-contract","severity":"MED","premise":"Build acceptance must qualify the chosen Avro library and physical schema for schema evolution, paging, recovery and committed-snapshot decoding rather than assume those capabilities already exist.","evidence":"The supplied duckdb.txt:1 read identifies src/daemon/db/duckdb-pool.ts:1–122 as a disposable in-memory query engine, not persistent storage. src/daemon/db/drivers/duckdb-file.ts:85–145 routes Avro through conversion to Parquet and read_parquet. src/daemon/db/drivers/converters/avro.ts:1–75 imports avsc and shows bounded decoding infrastructure, but does not establish schema evolution, paging, recovery, or committed-snapshot decoding. The truncated grep supplies no qualification results for those capabilities. The acceptance requirement is therefore prudent but unverifiable from this evidence.","action":"Supply acceptance criteria and qualification results for the chosen Avro library and physical schema covering schema evolution, paging, recovery, and committed-snapshot decoding.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence establishes the existing conversion/query path but cannot verify the proposed storage capabilities or their acceptance coverage.","options":["Attach qualification tests and results covering all four capabilities.","Reword the premise as an explicit pending qualification requirement, citing the existing Avro-to-Parquet path only as background."]}},{"claimId":"p51","ref":"2/S004:FR002","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A daemon DuckDB query layer exists as an integration target for committed accounting report snapshots.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/duckdb.txt:1 reproduces src/daemon/db/duckdb-pool.ts:1-122, establishing a daemon-owned in-memory query engine for file-backed queries, with getDuckDB() initialization and withConnection<T>(fn) identified as the canonical query entry point. The same read includes src/daemon/db/drivers/duckdb-file.ts:85-145, which maps Parquet and converted file kinds to read_parquet(?). This confirms an existing query-layer integration target; it does not establish existing accounting snapshot compatibility or persistence, neither of which the premise claims.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p52","ref":"7/c9","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The code evidence cited as c9 resolves at line 21 of the token-usage review evidence document.","evidence":"The supplied read of plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:21 resolves to `c9 | Source src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts`, confirming that c9 is at the cited line.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p53","ref":"7/c10","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The code evidence cited as c10 resolves at line 23 of the token-usage review evidence document.","evidence":"The supplied read of plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:23 resolves to the c10 entry, identifying src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts and including its journal implementation. This confirms the cited location.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p54","ref":"7/c15","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The stakeholder root-storage decision cited as c15 resolves at the first line of the root-storage decision JSON file.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-root-storage-decision.json:1 resolves to the decision JSON, identifying its source as an explicit user architecture correction and recording the root-storage request.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":10,"low":44},"reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T06:41:42.579Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
